UI/UX IMPROVEMENT PROMPT — EXISTING YATIN PATIL PORTFOLIO

Improve the existing Yatin Patil portfolio design rather than completely redesigning it.

Keep the current overall visual direction:

Bright + minimal + professional + editorial + technical + human

Keep the existing strong typography, warm off-white background, charcoal text, thin borders and subtle blue accent.

The goal is to make the existing portfolio feel more intentional, interactive, visually rich and premium, while preserving its clean aesthetic.

Do NOT turn it into a dark developer portfolio, generic SaaS website, dashboard, or overly animated AI portfolio.

1. FIX THE HERO SECTION

The current hero has too much unused empty space on the right.

Keep the large headline on the left, but introduce a meaningful interactive visual system on the right.

Do NOT simply add a decorative 3D object.

Create a visual that represents my way of thinking:

PROBLEM → DATA → MODEL → PRODUCT

Use a clean editorial diagram.

For example:

        PROBLEM
           ↓
         DATA
           ↓
         MODEL
           ↓
        PRODUCT

Place the nodes organically rather than as a boring vertical flowchart.

Use thin connecting lines.

Use small blue accent points.

When hovering over a node:

Node expands slightly
Connection line becomes visible
Short explanation appears
Related technology/project appears

Example:

DATA

"Finding patterns that actually matter."

MODEL

"Testing different approaches instead of assuming the first one works."

PRODUCT

"Turning the technical solution into something usable."

Keep this visual subtle and premium.

2. MAKE THE HERO FEEL LESS EMPTY

Use the available right-side space intentionally.

Add a small editorial information block near the interactive system:

CURRENTLY BUILDING

AI / DATA / SOFTWARE

Then underneath:

3+ ongoing experiments

Do NOT use fake statistics.

If exact numbers are unknown, use:

Selected experiments

instead.

Add a tiny vertical line or blue indicator.

The right side should feel designed, not filled with random decoration.

3. IMPROVE HERO TYPOGRAPHY

Keep:

I build things that turn problems into products.

But refine the hierarchy.

Make:

problems

and

products

slightly emphasized using the blue accent or subtle weight difference.

Do not make the entire headline blue.

The headline should remain predominantly charcoal.

Use a controlled line length so the heading feels intentional rather than simply wrapping because of the container width.

4. IMPROVE THE INTRODUCTION

Current:

I'm Yatin — an Information Technology student exploring AI/ML, data science and software development...

Improve the presentation.

Keep the content, but break it into:

WHO I AM

I'm Yatin — an Information Technology student exploring AI/ML, data science and software development through real projects, experiments and constant iteration.

Then add small metadata:

AI / ML

DATA

SOFTWARE

These should behave as interactive tags.

5. IMPROVE CTA BUTTONS

Current buttons are functional but generic.

Keep:

Explore my work ↓

About me ↗

Improve their interaction.

Explore my work

Default:

Dark charcoal background.

Hover:

Background transitions toward cobalt blue
Arrow moves slightly downward/right
Button expands subtly
Section preview appears
About me

Default:

Transparent/off-white background.

Hover:

Border becomes blue
Arrow moves right
Text becomes blue

Keep the buttons rectangular and premium.

Do not turn them into large pill buttons.

6. CREATE A STRONG TRANSITION AFTER HERO

The page currently moves from the hero into another section without enough narrative transition.

Add a small editorial statement:

I don't just show the final result.
I show the thinking behind it.

Below:

PROBLEM → APPROACH → BUILD → RESULT → LEARNING

This should become a signature element of the website.

7. MAKE THE PROCESS INTERACTIVE

Turn:

PROBLEM / APPROACH / BUILD / RESULT / LEARNING

into five interactive steps.

Desktop:

Display horizontally.

Each step has:

01
PROBLEM

02
APPROACH

03
BUILD

04
RESULT

05
LEARNING

On hover:

Step becomes slightly larger
Blue line appears underneath
Short description fades in
Connecting line animates

On click:

Expand the selected item.

This should be one of the most important UX interactions on the site.

8. IMPROVE THE CURRENTLY EXPLORING SECTION

The current:

AI / ML | Data Science | Computer Vision | LLMs | Full Stack | UI/UX

looks too much like a row of buttons.

Keep the same content but redesign it as an interactive exploration system.

Use large typography:

Currently exploring

Then create:

AI / ML
Data Science
Computer Vision
LLMs
Full Stack
UI/UX

Each item should have a subtle number:

01

02

03

etc.

On hover:

The item expands.

A small description appears.

Example:

Computer Vision

"Exploring how machine learning can extract useful information from images."

LLMs

"Learning how retrieval, embeddings and language models work together."

UI/UX

"Designing interfaces that make technical systems easier to understand."

Only one item should be expanded at a time.

